  "youtube": {
    "title": "Why Your Brain Won't Shut Up At Night #shorts",
    "description": "Lying awake running the same to-do list on repeat? Your brain holds onto unfinished tasks (the Zeigarnik effect). It isn't trying to annoy you. It's scared you'll forget.\n\nThe fix is weirdly simple: write tomorrow's to-do list before bed. In a sleep study, people who did this fell asleep about 9 minutes faster than people who wrote about what they'd already finished.\n\nResearch: Scullin et al. (2018), Journal of Experimental Psychology: General.\n\n#shorts #sleep #overthinking #psychology #productivity #animation #selfimprovement",
